  recipeId: thermal
  concept: 'Authored objective: Pass thermal endurance.

    Authored requirement:
    Run the controlled workload and ambient cycles with in-range thermal and memory
    evidence.

    General teaching principle: Thermal control depends on measured
    temperatures, loads, feedback and operating limits over time.

    Only fresh,
    authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A thermostat illustrates the need to distinguish a measured condition
    from a chosen setpoint.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A fan command by itself does not prove that thermal protection is
    effective.
